[h1]Transport Fever 2 Multiplayer[/h1][i]Mod version: 0.6.1.14 -- free and open source (MIT)[/i]
Play Transport Fever 2 together. Several players build roads, railways, stations, depots, vehicles and lines in [b]one shared world at the same time[/b]. Everything one player builds appears for everyone, at the same moment of the simulation on every machine. Play one company together, or give every player a company of their own on the same map.
[hr][/hr]
[h2]This Workshop Item Is a Signpost[/h2]The mod needs native components beside the game (a few DLLs and a small lobby program) that the Workshop cannot deliver, so [b]subscribing here installs nothing that plays[/b]. Subscribing is harmless: the item does nothing when enabled, and a save that lists it loads everywhere. The mod itself comes from the website:
[url=https://silver2127.github.io/tpf2-multiplayer/]silver2127.github.io/tpf2-multiplayer[/url]
[hr][/hr]
[h2]Early Access Notice[/h2]The game has no network code of its own; this mod adds lockstep multiplayer from outside, reverse-engineered without the engine's source. It is [b]experimental[/b]: expect the occasional desync, a build that does not replicate, or a crash, especially in long sessions on big maps. Keep your own saves. Sessions of up to four players have been run, on one PC and across the internet. Bug reports with logs are very welcome.
[hr][/hr]
[h2]Installation[/h2][b]Windows (Steam version of the game)[/b]
[olist][*] Download [b]TpF2Multiplayer.msi[/b] from the [url=https://github.com/silver2127/tpf2-multiplayer/releases/latest]latest release[/url]
[*] Close the game and run it; it finds the game folder through Steam
[*] Start the game: the title menu has a new [b]MULTIPLAYER[/b] button[/olist][b]Linux and Steam Deck (the Windows game under Proton)[/b]
[olist][*] In Steam, set the game to run with Proton 9 or newer, start it once and quit
[*] Download [b]install_proton.sh[/b] from the same release page and run [b]sh install_proton.sh[/b][/olist]Every player needs the [b]same mod version[/b]. A new version is installed the same way, over the old one; there is no in-game updater. Uninstall from Windows Apps, or run the installer again and choose Remove.
[hr][/hr]
[h2]How to Play[/h2][olist][*] Title menu, [b]MULTIPLAYER[/b], [b]HOST GAME[/b]. The join code is on your clipboard: send it to your friends, or tick [b]PUBLIC[/b] to list the game. A password locks the code.
[*] Friends open [b]MULTIPLAYER[/b], paste the code and press [b]JOIN GAME[/b], or click your game under [b]PUBLIC GAMES[/b].
[*] The host presses [b]START GAME[/b]. The host's newest save goes to everyone, mods included; then everyone opens [b]LOAD GAME[/b] and picks [b]mp_shared[/b].
[*] Build.[/olist]A new game has the multiplayer mod enabled by itself; for an existing save, enable it once in the save's Mods panel. The host should have UDP port 29471 reachable (the lobby tries UPnP). If that is not possible, play on the [b]public dedicated test server[/b] in PUBLIC GAMES, where nobody needs an open port. It runs all day.
[hr][/hr]
[h2]Features[/h2][list][*] [b]One shared world[/b]: every build, purchase, sale, line edit and demolition applies at the same simulation step on every machine
[*] [b]Shared company or one company per player[/b]: co-op in one company, or the host's SEPARATE COMPANIES option gives every player a company with its own money
[*] [b]Hot join[/b]: a player can join a running game; the session holds while they load
[*] [b]Automatic save and mod transfer[/b] to every joiner, over a fast direct channel
[*] [b]Works through home routers[/b]: hole punching first, a relay when the punch cannot work
[*] [b]Public game list and join codes[/b], with an optional password
[*] [b]Session speed by vote[/b]: the average of everyone's votes; a pause is a pause for everyone
[*] [b]Desync detection[/b] with a one-click resync from the host's save
[*] [b]Dedicated server[/b]: a headless host that keeps a world up for anyone to join
[*] [b]Nothing phones home[/b]: no telemetry, no statistics, no crash upload ([url=https://silver2127.github.io/tpf2-multiplayer/privacy.html]privacy policy[/url])[/list]
[hr][/hr]
[h2]Requirements[/h2][list][*] Transport Fever 2 on Steam, build 35924 (Windows, or Linux / Steam Deck through Proton)
[*] The same mod version on every player's PC
[*] For a host: UDP port 29471 reachable, or use the dedicated server[/list]
[hr][/hr]
[h2]Compatible Mods[/h2][b]Compatible[/b]
[list][*] [url=https://github.com/silver2127/tpf2-bigmap]TpF2 Big Maps[/url] -- maps far beyond the game's size limit, from the same author; the two install alongside each other in either order, and a Big Maps world plays like any other[/list][b]Not yet compatible[/b]
[list][*] [b]Natural Town Growth[/b] and similar mods that change how towns grow or drive the simulation from a script. Their changes run on each player's game separately and drift apart, so the worlds desync. I am working on it.[/list]Most other mods are fine: vehicles, buildings, stations, tracks, roads, assets and visual mods load the same way for everyone. The host's save decides a session's mods, and they are sent to the joiners automatically. If a mod desyncs a session, please report it by name.
[hr][/hr]
[h2]Troubleshooting[/h2]Most problems are fixed by a [b]rejoin[/b] or a [b]resync[/b] (when the Multiplayer window shows DESYNC, press [b]Resync now[/b] at its top: the host's save is reloaded on every machine). Before reporting a bug:
[list][*] Make sure every player runs the same mod version; the lobby refuses a different one
[*] Have the affected player leave and join again
[*] If nobody can connect to you, check the host's port or use the dedicated server
[*] Steam's "Verify integrity of game files" removes the mod's hook; the installer's Repair brings the MULTIPLAYER button back[/list][b]Known Issues[/b]
[list][*] [b]A player far behind the others[/b] has their actions held until they catch up; wait, or lower the speed
[*] [b]A second game on the same PC[/b] does not get the hooks
[*] [b]A four-arm track crossing built as one piece[/b] freezes the game; build it as two straight lines
[*] [b]Some stop and line details do not replicate yet[/b]; the full list is in KNOWN_ISSUES.md on GitHub[/list]If a problem persists, open an [url=https://github.com/silver2127/tpf2-multiplayer/issues]issue on GitHub[/url] with a short description and the logs from [b]%LOCALAPPDATA%\tpf2mp\logs[/b]. Logs from everyone involved speed things up enormously.
[hr][/hr]
